kant-groundwork-3.md:1: argue/readings: the conclusion is read 3 ways: kant-groundwork-3.logic.r2 has "∀x (violates_strict(x) ∨ violates_lax(x) → unwillable(x))"; kant-groundwork-3.logic.r2.2 has "∀x (unwillable(x) → violates_strict(x) ∨ violates_lax(x))"; they differ when nothing is true, which the first allows; kant-groundwork-3.logic.r2.3 has "∀x ((inconceivable(x) → violates_strict(x) ∧ ¬permissible(x)) ∧ (unwillable(x) ∧ ¬inconceivable(x) → violates_lax(x) ∧ ¬permissible(x)))"
