kant-groundwork-3.md:1: argue/quantifier: kant-groundwork-3.logic.r2 P2 (S1): the sentence says "few", but P2 says all: it reads "for every x, if (either action x violates strict or rigorous (inflexible) duty or action x violates laxer (meritorious) duty), then (either the maxim of action x cannot without contradiction be even conceived as a universal law of nature or (it is not so that the maxim of action x cannot without contradiction be even conceived as a universal law of nature and it is impossible to will that the maxim of action x should be a universal law))"
